# mem2 OUTPUT: what your part must produce

## 1. Kafka topic `market-ticks` (consumed by mem3's Bronze ticks sink)
Key = `ticker`, 3 partitions, about 100 messages/s in total (10 tickers x 10/s). Only `emitted_at` changes between consecutive messages of a ticker until the next yfinance poll:
```json
{"ticker":"RELIANCE","price":1425.30,"volume":4200000,"price_as_of":"2026-11-09T04:30:00Z","emitted_at":"2026-11-09T04:45:00.100Z","market_open":true,"source":"yfinance"}
{"ticker":"RELIANCE","price":1425.30,"volume":4200000,"price_as_of":"2026-11-09T04:30:00Z","emitted_at":"2026-11-09T04:45:00.200Z","market_open":true,"source":"yfinance"}
```
Rules: price is the real yfinance value, never rounded, jittered or simulated; all 10 tickers every cycle; `market_open=false` outside NSE hours.

## 2. Silver ticks: `data_path('silver','ticks')` (read by mem4)
One row per VALID tick, format `storage.table_format`, append, checkpoint `silver_ticks`:
```text
ticker    price    volume   price_as_of           emitted_at               market_open is_new_price
RELIANCE  1425.30  4200000  2026-11-09T04:30:00Z  2026-11-09T04:45:00.100Z true        true
RELIANCE  1425.30  4200000  2026-11-09T04:30:00Z  2026-11-09T04:45:00.200Z true        false
INFY      1610.75  3100000  2026-11-09T04:30:00Z  2026-11-09T04:45:00.100Z true        true
```
Rejected (not written): null/<=0 price, ticker outside the 10, malformed JSON, unparsable timestamps. Audit proof: exactly one price per (ticker, price_as_of).

## 3. Audit rows (via `common.audit`)
`silver_processing_audit` (one row per micro-batch; **input_count = processed_count + rejected_count**):
```text
run_id=20261109T044500-d4e5f6 job_name=silver_ticks_job batch_id=812 input_count=500 processed_count=498 rejected_count=2 ticker_count=10 duration_ms=900 status=OK
```
`pipeline_execution_audit` rows for `price_poller`, `tick_publisher` and `silver_ticks_job` (status RUNNING with heartbeat, STOPPED/FAILED on exit; records_processed, throughput_per_sec, error_count).

## 4. The dashboard (Streamlit, reads Postgres)
Screens: (1) KPIs: tickers monitored, windows, articles, alerts; (2) per-ticker chart: price (INR) line + sentiment bars; (3) alert feed, newest first, with reason; (4) pipeline health: msgs/sec, newest event time, rows per layer; (5) audit tables (4 tables, latest 20 rows each). All times IST, prices INR. Auto-refresh about 5 s; shows an honest note when `market_open=false`.

## How to verify your output
`python scripts/peek.py silver/ticks` · `python scripts/verify_pipeline.py` ("REAL PRICES ONLY" must PASS, lineage Silver ⊆ Bronze) · `streamlit run dashboard/app.py`.
